From: adorfer <adorferen@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gluon-mesh-vpn-tunneldigger: watchdog does not restart without WAN IPv4

Port of Neanderfunk FirmwareConfigs v2023.2.x e362e4d to Gluon v2021.1.x.

Without an IPv4 address on br-wan tunneldigger reaches no broker (the client
is IPv4 only). The watchdog then restarted it every 5 minutes and set up the
same failing loop again (WDR3600 without WAN, LAN mesh only). With an address
everything stays as before; the pid-file check is unchanged (a dead or
duplicate process is restarted with or without WAN).

---
--- a/package/gluon-mesh-vpn-tunneldigger/luasrc/usr/bin/tunneldigger-watchdog
+++ b/package/gluon-mesh-vpn-tunneldigger/luasrc/usr/bin/tunneldigger-watchdog
@@ -38,6 +38,15 @@
 		restart_tunneldigger()
 		return
 	end
+	-- Without an IPv4 address on br-wan no broker is reachable (the client is
+	-- IPv4 only); a restart would just set up the same failing loop again.
+	-- Neanderfunk, port of FirmwareConfigs v2023.2.x e362e4d.
+	local wan = io.popen('ip -4 addr show dev br-wan 2>/dev/null')
+	local has_ipv4 = wan:read('*a'):find('inet ') ~= nil
+	wan:close()
+	if not has_ipv4 then
+		return
+	end
 	if not has_mesh_vpn_neighbours() then
 		os.execute('logger -t tunneldigger-watchdog "No vpn-mesh neighbours found."')
 		restart_tunneldigger()
